{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/144043-wraith-chronicle-starters","id":144043,"title":"Wraith chronicle starters?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-20T20:17:21-07:00","id":144043,"title":"Wraith chronicle starters?","content":"I'm looking at running Wraith sometime very soon, which is all very exciting. My only concern is that I need some sort of plot that keeps the circle together, and I don't want to have very much of the Hierarchy/Heretics/Renegades in this chronicle; the circle and their (un)lives and Passions are the star of the show, with a few other local wraiths, spectres, and mortals being focused on. What are good mens of keeping the player characters together? I was considering a common origin (all were killed by the same serial killer, all comitted suicide, etc) but can't think of something interesting enough to give a chronicle steam. Help!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T00:17:26-07:00","id":144232,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">The Hierarchy can be portrayed as consistently or as inconsistently as you want it. Some Anacreons enforce every Stygian law with an iron fist. Others may have a more laissez-faire approach; don\u2019t f* with us and we won\u2019t f* with you. Some Renegades aren\u2019t about bringing down the man. They just want to do their own thing with no interference. No all Heretics are hyper-religious zealots; some may be groups that heard about Transcendence and think it\u2019s a good thing to strive for. <br /> <br /> In the Necropolis, represent the three \u2018factions\u2019 as more moderate. Not Utopian, mind you, just less douchey. <br /> <br /> People don\u2019t have to be BFFs to be in a Circle. Don\u2019t get me wrong, you don\u2019t want them racking up Angst while they try shoving each other in a Nihil, but they can be a small group of dead people who get along jus\u2019 cuz. [I think many people have friends like this\u2026]<br /> <br /> The following are some examples from my troupe\u2019s Circle. For ideas, why not.<br /> <br /> My troupe\u2019s Circle consisted of:<br /> <br /> Couch-potato-turned-Doomed-Reaper (Legion of Fate)<br /> Raver-turned-vampire-hunter (Renegade\u2026ish)<br /> Trucker-turned-Ferryman-wannabe (Heretic\u2026ish)<br /> <br /> The Circle didn\u2019t share a Haunt, a common background, or even manner of death; they just got along. Also having different affiliations lead to some interesting story twists. <br /> <br /> Escapade Recap:<br /> <br /> After we (finally) tracked down the vampire who killed our raver friend, he used Embody to cross the Shroud and take him on in an Ectoplasmic versus Undead showdown. When it was over, the raver had a quiet moment of peace as one of his Passions became closer to being Resolved. It was nice little denouement. At the end of the scene, however, we found ourselves corned by a patrol lead by an overzealous centurion (a reoccurring character). He arrested the raver and the trucker [he didn\u2019t want the headache of actually arresting a Stygian official, but I was still forcibly encouraged to be \u2018escorted\u2019] for violation of the Dictum Mortuum. The next session, while my Circlemates were in manacles, I had to convince said centurion that my friends hadn\u2019t actually broken any Stygian laws. It was a more entertaining way to finish up the story then ending it with a, \u201cI beat him!\u201d </span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-21T10:47:10-07:00","id":144619,"title":"","content":"I had the circle start out with the same death. They all died in a plane crash. Later on they found out they had different deathmarks, so there was weirdness. <br /> <br /> Since they all had the same death, they all had the same Reaper, who was important later, but he told them to run as the slavers were on their way. Running off was a bonding experience for some very different traumatized people. Their differences were less important than their shared circumstances to start with. So, good Circle cohesion before the differences started to show.<br /> <br /> I did have an overall plot and had really mined the history of the city to set up who the movers and shakers were. I guess it was Hierarchy oriented (mostly b/c they were best supported with supplements). Lots of thinking about what each Legion DID in the city. So they had different areas of influence divided up.The players all got associated with the Emerald Legion to begin with, but they were relatively nice, easy-going fellows, relatively speaking.<br /> <br /> A lot happened. It worked. We had a ton of fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}